{% doc %}
  The count classes for a grid of cards, so no card sits alone on a row (DESIGN.md §6.5): four or
  eight go two, then four across (DS-44); a count that would leave a short last row at three across
  gives the spare room to its first two cards (lead, DS-52); an odd count at two across starts with
  one wide card (odd, DS-52); a card alone takes the spare room, its picture beside its text
  (single, DS-74, DS-92). Every grid of cards uses it, so they all follow one rule: card groups,
  the lesson lists (gs-lesson-list, More lessons), the Past exhibition list, More
  exhibitions, an artist's exhibitions and the collection's ways in. gs-grid-sizes gives the
  matching sizes for each card's picture.

  @param {number} count - How many cards

  @example
  {%- capture mods -%}{% render 'gs-grid-modifiers', count: ids.size %}{%- endcapture -%}
  <ul class="gs-grid gs-grid--cards{{ mods | strip_newlines }}" role="list">
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign by_three = count | modulo: 3
  assign by_four = count | modulo: 4
  assign by_two = count | modulo: 2
  assign fours = false
  if by_four == 0 and by_three != 0
    assign fours = true
    echo ' gs-grid--fours'
  endif
  if fours == false and by_three == 2
    echo ' gs-grid--lead'
  endif
  if count > 1 and by_two == 1
    echo ' gs-grid--odd'
  endif
  if count == 1
    echo ' gs-grid--single'
  endif
-%}
